The files in this directory are the ref10 Ed25519 implementation from:

    https://github.com/orlp/ed25519
    Copyright (c) 2015 Orson Peters <orsonpeters@gmail.com>
    zlib license (see below)

They are vendored unmodified. Two consumers share them:

- adbwire's SPAKE2 implementation (../spake2.c) uses the field/group/scalar
  arithmetic (fe.c, ge.c, sc.c, precomp_data.h) to interoperate with
  Android's Wireless Debugging pairing, which uses BoringSSL's
  SPAKE2-over-Ed25519 (crypto/curve25519/spake25519.cc).
- relaysh's asymmetric auth (../../relaysh) uses the higher-level files
  (sha512.c, keypair.c, sign.c, verify.c, key_exchange.c, ed25519.h) for
  client ed25519 signatures and ephemeral X25519-style ECDH. Verified against
  the RFC 8032 section 7.1 TEST 1 vector plus an ECDH agreement test before
  use. seed.c is intentionally NOT vendored - seed material comes from
  relaysh_random(), so no `randombytes` dependency is pulled in.

